---
name: dev-sanity-task
version: 2.20.1
description: lead sanity check assignment for the member that fills the dev-sanity role (resolve-role dev-sanity). task_id is the sanity check bead. The member splits the checked bead per numbered deliverable (sanity-split), runs LLM and JEV checkers per deliverable and a selected merge with lint alongside, then reports PASS or FAIL. Not QA.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - checked_bead
  - sprint
  - worktree_path
  - base
  - pr_url
  - primary_checkout
  - lint_command
  - beads_dir
  - close_context
defaults:
  base_verified: false
  base_source: ""
  nr: false
  sanity_close_mode: "legacy"
  qa_task_id: ""
  sanity_task_id: ""
  dev_task_id: ""
  pr_number: ""
  commit: ""
  branch: ""
  layer_prs: []
metadata:
  type: dev-sanity-task
  tags:
    - stage:dev-sanity
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: dev-sanity-start
    stage: dev-sanity
    transition: start
---
{% set task_id = sanity_task_id if sanity_task_id else task_id %}
{% set base_nonhex = base | string | lower | replace('0', '') | replace('1', '') | replace('2', '') | replace('3', '') | replace('4', '') | replace('5', '') | replace('6', '') | replace('7', '') | replace('8', '') | replace('9', '') | replace('a', '') | replace('b', '') | replace('c', '') | replace('d', '') | replace('e', '') | replace('f', '') %}
{% if (base | string | length) != 40 or base_nonhex %}{{ base | dispatcher_must_supply_full_40_hex_base }}{% endif %}
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" mode="dev-sanity" close-mode="{{ sanity_close_mode }}">
  <description><![CDATA[Sanity check `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`: each numbered deliverable is written; lint passes. The base is the layer's parent commit and the only diff base. This is not QA.]]></description>

  <checked-bead><![CDATA[{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}]]></checked-bead>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <base><![CDATA[{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}]]></base>
  <base-verified>{% if base_verified %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}</base-verified>
  <base-source><![CDATA[{{ base_source | string | cdata_escape }}]]></base-source>
  <not-reproducible>{% if nr %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}</not-reproducible>
  <layer-prs><![CDATA[{{ layer_prs | join(" ") | string | cdata_escape }}]]></layer-prs>
  <pr number="{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}"><![CDATA[{{ pr_url | string | cdata_escape }}]]></pr>
  <lint-command><![CDATA[{{ lint_command | string | cdata_escape }}]]></lint-command>
  <beads-dir><![CDATA[{{ beads_dir | string | cdata_escape }}]]></beads-dir>
  <close-context><![CDATA[{{ close_context | tojson | cdata_escape }}]]></close-context>
  <workflow>
{% if sanity_close_mode == "daemon" %}
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Export BEADS_DIR={{ beads_dir | string | cdata_escape }}. At task_ready, run atm task start {{ task_id }} "Check each numbered deliverable" and claim with bd update {{ task_id }} --claim --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY". Before inspecting any PR, deliverable, or review evidence, capture the binding: read `atm task events {{ task_id }} --json`, select the newest assigned/reassigned/reopened event by sequence, and take its message_id (or seq if absent) as assignment_id; read `bd show {{ checked_bead }} --json` and take metadata.commit as commit. Capture the assigned <base> full 40-hex SHA. Save all three exact values to scratch/sanity-binding.json together and do not overwrite it during this review. Required planning fields are enforced by bd-validation; do not add a commit-freeze gate or manual dispatch checklist. An assignment conflict or failed verification command must be escalated to the phase lead with the exact records/error and recovery action; never wait silently. Produce the selected-result JSON in step b. No split manifest is required and no build-running split/merge helper may run.]]></step>
{% else %}
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Export BEADS_DIR={{ beads_dir | string | cdata_escape }}. Run {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/assignment-gates.py sanity --bead {{ task_id }} --commit {{ commit }} --worktree {{ worktree_path }}. Do not run a separate bd ready or bd show. READY: claim with bd update {{ task_id }} --claim --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY", then atm task start {{ task_id }} "Check each numbered deliverable". NOT_READY: diagnose with bd show {{ task_id }} --json and bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'; for each reported blocker run bd show <blocker> --json. Do not claim or start. Close refused with task-refused.md.j2, bead_state open, and reason_md naming the bead, the blocker or status, who must move it, and any missing edge bd dep add {{ task_id }} --blocked-by <blocker>. GATE_CANNOT_RUN: close refused with the exact gate command and failure evidence in reason_md; leave the bead open. Do not run bd ready separately. Copy <close-context> unchanged to scratch/close-context.json; pass it to sanity-split with --close-context. The split manifest carries all close fields and bead notes; never build or edit close vars by hand.]]></step>
{% endif %}
{% if sanity_close_mode == "daemon" %}
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Verify the numbered deliverables and the dev's existing build/test evidence for the implementation being reviewed. Inspect only each PR in <layer-prs> using its baseRefOid...headRefOid diff; if empty, use the single range from <base> to the current implementation head. Use the immutable values from scratch/sanity-binding.json for assignment_id and commit; do not refresh either value while preparing or selecting review results. These values bind the selected result to the assignment and implementation that were current before verification began. Sanity does not build: do not invoke Cargo, the lint or test commands, or a split/merge helper that launches them. Preserve completed review reports. Missing or stale dev evidence is a FAIL item for the dev, but only after reading the evidence the dev supplied (completion report, linked logs, final-tree manifest); scoped checks after a rebase that the quality policy allows count, and a full-suite run on the final head is not required. Produce the selected-result JSON with task_id={{ task_id }}, reviewer=sanity-selected, assignment_id, checked_bead={{ checked_bead }}, commit, base copied verbatim from the captured assignment <base>, base_verified={% if base_verified %}true{% else %}false{% endif %} copied from <base-verified>, base_source copied from <base-source>, nr copied from <not-reproducible>, a nonempty run_id, verdict PASS or FAIL, and findings as an array of {deliverable: <number>, issue: <reason>}; use deliverable 0 for a verification-wide evidence deficiency. PASS requires no findings; FAIL requires at least one. Include findings_md and lint_md describing only evidence actually inspected. If a conflicting assignment prevents identifying the target, a required review service is unavailable, or a verification tool fails, escalate the concrete conflicting records or failed operation/error to the phase lead. Do not fabricate a verdict or substitute CANNOT_RUN.]]></step>
{% else %}
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Follow `.claude/agents/dev-sanity.md`, the canonical coordinator. Run sanity-split once, with `--layer-pr <n>` for each PR in `<layer-prs>` (empty: the single range from `<base>`) and `--external-evidence <json>` for each extra evidence reference (such as a `pr_comment`), and send identical assignments to both reviewers concurrently. Keep both raw result arrays; a JEV reply's `data.jev` comes only from `wrap_jev_receipt.py`. When a reviewer's last reply or timeout envelope arrives, record its completion epoch before merging or waiting for shared lint, then merge it immediately with `--started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch>`. Append no history until selected merge sets the final verdict. Build one strict selection array, one entry per deliverable; record the selected start epoch when selection begins and completion epoch when `selection.json` is written. Invoke selected merge only as `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/sanity-merge ... --reviewer sanity-selected --started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch> --llm-vars <sanity-llm-vars.json> --jev-vars <sanity-jev-vars.json> --selection <selection.json>`; it ignores stdin. Append history in exact order `sanity-llm`, then `sanity-jev`, both rows with the selected verdict as `--final-verdict`; if selection or selected merge cannot run, use `CANNOT_RUN` and still append LLM/JEV. Retain selected vars unchanged as the --vars input to atm task close; the daemon hook resolves task and bead context. Exit 4: wait for shared lint; retries reuse supplied epochs. Selected cannot-run routes to e2.]]></step>
{% endif %}
{% if sanity_close_mode == "daemon" %}
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Immediately before close, re-read `atm task events {{ task_id }} --json` and `bd show {{ checked_bead }} --json`. Confirm scratch/sanity-binding.json and the selected result still contain the captured assignment_id and commit, and that both still match the newest assignment and current metadata.commit. If either changed, do not update or submit the selected result under the new values; discard it and restart the review from the beginning with a newly captured binding (or escalate if the assignment is no longer yours). Then run `atm task close {{ task_id }} completed --template {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/sanity-task-close.md.j2 --vars <selected-vars.json>`. This is the only close command: do not invoke atm-task-close.py or manually close beads. The registered sanity hook validates assignment_id and commit against current task history and checked bead before journaling. FAIL carries its findings exactly as step b selected them, `[{deliverable, issue}]` (never `undone`, `number` or `reason`). PASS and FAIL are the only accepted verdicts. Sanity does not build: missing deliverables or missing/stale dev evidence are FAIL. Assignment conflicts, unavailable required review services, and verification-tool failures require escalation with exact conflicting records or failed operation/error. Legacy CANNOT_RUN is rejected with an explicit lead escalation. Validation errors name an owner and correlation ID; report the error to the phase lead with the failed operation and recovery direction; correct the result or required bead data at its source, then retry close. Bead writes are journaled in bd-cache and applied by its drain; a write that cannot be applied is escalated to the phase lead by the bd-cache cron, so never retry bead writes. For a fixed PASS, only after successful close, prepare stack-input.json with checked_bead, branch, commit, pr_number, worktree_path, and stack_bead/budget/lead from current task/bead context (phase_lead supplies lead); hand that input to sanity-stack. For not_reproducible PASS, skip stacking.]]></step>
{% else %}
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Run {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/sanity-close-vars --manifest <manifest.json> --selected <selected-vars.json> --stack-input <stack-input.json> > <close-vars.json>. Run {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/atm-task-close.py --role sanity --vars <close-vars.json> immediately on the selected verdict, without waiting for any stack result. For a fixed PASS, hand <stack-input.json> unchanged to sanity-stack only after successful close, or run sanity-stack-link --input <stack-input.json> after the close. The generated stack input carries the stack bead and phase lead. For a not_reproducible PASS, no stack input is produced and no stack handoff runs. stack_failed, lock_timeout or rebase_required is notified by sanity-stack-link to the phase lead; this sanity task stays closed and no sanity round is counted for stack outcomes. FAIL retains selected undone numbers and reasons; CANNOT_RUN refuses through the hook. On hook err fix the named cause and rerun with the generated vars; never hand-edit them.]]></step>
{% endif %}
    <step id="e2"><![CDATA[{% if sanity_close_mode == "daemon" %}Do not submit CANNOT_RUN. Missing deliverables or missing/stale evidence are FAIL and return to the dev. For an assignment conflict, required review-service outage, or verification-tool failure, report the exact records or failed operation/error and responsible owner to the phase lead. Keep the task open for that escalation; do not invent a verdict. A bead write that cannot be applied after a validated PASS/FAIL is escalated by bd-cache, not by you; the original task still closes.{% else %}A blocker is not a failure: when a prerequisite reopens or work needs an unlanded fix, never stay active waiting. Record BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why> and any missing edge bd dep add {{ task_id }} --blocked-by <blocker>. Run the legacy hook with verdict CANNOT_RUN; it returns the bead open and unassigned and refuses the task.{% endif %}]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[After the hook closes this task and the post-close stack handoff is dispatched, read ATM again. The console runs tabs replace the chat status table.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
